%N A400948 Primes p such that (p-1)/2 is either prime or a squarefree semiprime.
%C A400948 These primes can be considered semisafe primes and are a superset of the safe primes.
%H A400948 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semiprime">Semiprime</a>.
%H A400948 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safe_and_Sophie_Germain_primes">Safe and Sophie Germain primes</a>.
%e A400948 11 is term because 11 is prime and 5 is a prime.
%e A400948 13 is term because 13 is prime and 6 is a squarefree semiprime.
%p A400948 q:= p-> isprime(p) and ifactors((p-1)/2)[2][.., 2] in {[1], [1,1]}:
%p A400948 select(q, [$3..700])[];  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Oct 10 2026
%t A400948 Table[If[k=(n-1)/2; PrimeQ[n]&&IntegerQ[k]&&k>1&&SquareFreeQ[k]&&Length@FactorInteger[k]<3, n, Nothing], {n, 1, 1000}]
%Y A400948 Cf. A005097, A005385, A006881, A063640.
%Y A400948 Union of A005385 and A063640 \ {19}.
